# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout and a Linux CI runner see the
# same bytes; this template is edited on Windows but its scripts run wherever
# a clone lands, and a silently mismatched EOL breaks Bash's `#!/bin/bash`
# shebang parsing (a CRLF script fails with "bad interpreter") while a batch
# file that isn't CRLF can fail to run under cmd.exe. So: text is normalized
# by default, shell scripts are forced to LF, Windows launchers to CRLF, and
# known binaries are marked so Git never attempts to diff or convert them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
